Prompt: evaluate_reading_power.j2
Service Step: EVALUATE_READING_POWER (Reading Power Evaluation)
Brief Description: Evaluate the reading power of a chapter, including end-of-chapter hooks, previous chapter hook fulfillment, micro-payoffs, and other dimensions.
Upstream Input:
  - chapter_number: Chapter number
  - genre: Genre type
  - chapter_type: Chapter type
  - previous_hook_description: Previous chapter hook description
  - expected_hook: Outline hook expectation (type/strength/description)
  - expected_payoffs: Outline micro-payoff expectation list
  - chapter_text: Chapter body text
  - suspense_timeline_entries: Cross-chapter suspense chain tracking entries
Downstream Output:
  - JSON: {"hook_type", "hook_strength", "hook_description", "prev_hook_fulfilled", ...}
  - Downstream Consumer: RepairStep / EvaluateStep
Consumption Chain Priority: P1 (Missing end-of-chapter hook / Previous chapter hook not responded) > P2 (Insufficient micro-payoffs / Transition chapter judgment)
Brief Example:
  Input: chapter_number=5, previous_hook_description="Protagonist surrounded"
  Output: {"hook_type": "crisis", "hook_strength": "strong", "prev_hook_fulfilled": true}
